ZCode CLI — attribution notice
==============================

Portions of this project are ported or adapted from opencode
(https://github.com/sst/opencode), licensed under the MIT License.
Reference checkout: branch `dev`, commit 7a8e7c88f.
A copy of the opencode license is kept at licenses/opencode-LICENSE.

Ported material is rewritten as plain async TypeScript (the original is
Effect-based); algorithms, prompt texts, and parameter choices originate
from the files listed below.

Per-file porting record
-----------------------

- src/llm/stream.ts
  GLM dialect handling (thinking enable flag, glm-5.2 reasoning-effort
  variants, reasoning_content round-trip on assistant messages, per-model
  temperature defaults) adapted from
  packages/opencode/src/provider/transform.ts.

- src/tools/edit/replacers.ts
  The multi-strategy replacer family and `replace()` fallback ladder
  (simple, line-trimmed, block-anchor, whitespace-normalized,
  indentation-flexible, escape-normalized, trimmed-boundary, context-aware,
  multi-occurrence) ported from packages/opencode/src/tool/edit.ts, which
  sources the algorithms from cline (evals/diff-edits) and gemini-cli
  (editCorrector).

- src/tools/read.ts, write.ts, edit.ts, bash.ts, grep.ts, glob.ts,
  webfetch.ts, todo.ts
  Tool behaviour (line-numbered read output, read-before-write constraint,
  ripgrep argument shapes, bash output tail-truncation, webfetch format
  negotiation) adapted from the matching packages/opencode/src/tool/*.ts.
  Effect wrappers removed; rewritten as plain async TypeScript.

- src/tools/prompts/{read,write,edit,grep,glob,webfetch,todowrite}.txt
  Verbatim tool description prompts copied from
  packages/opencode/src/tool/*.txt. (bash.txt is written for ZCode CLI.)

- src/agent/compact.ts
  The context-summarization system prompt is adapted from
  packages/opencode/src/agent/prompt/compaction.txt; the append-only
  compaction/projection approach follows opencode's session/compaction.ts.
